---
// `/search` moved to `/takes`. The tab lists takes and always did — searching
// is how you narrow them, not what they are — so the route now matches the
// object, and sits beside `/takes/[id]` the way `/songs` sits beside
// `/songs/[slug]`.
//
// This redirect exists because links to the old path are already out in the
// world: `/me`'s unvoted count shipped pointing at `/search?unvoted=1` earlier
// today, and a member may have bookmarked a filtered search. 301, not 302 —
// the move is permanent, and a permanent redirect lets a browser stop asking.
// The query string is carried through verbatim, so a saved filter still lands
// on the same results rather than on an empty archive.
const target = `/takes${Astro.url.search}`;
return Astro.redirect(target, 301);
---
